<title>ITALY: Olivetti CEO Caio has resigned - state tv.</title>
<headline>Olivetti CEO Caio has resigned - state tv.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Olivetti chief executive officer Francesco Caio is reported to have resigned and is being replaced by Roberto Colaninno, a close associate of the group's former chairman Carlo De Benedetti, Italian state television reported.</p>
<p>The report said Caio had resigned at an extraordinary board meeting. Olivetti's share price has plunged in recent days before recovering in advance of the board meeting.</p>
<p>Colaninno is currently managing director of automotive components group Sogefi. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
